---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import LPageHead from '../components/liquid/PageHead.astro';
import { glass } from '../theme';
---

<Base title="Privacy notice" description={`How ${site.name} handles the information you share through this site.`}>
  {
    glass ? (
      <LPageHead eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy notice." drops={false} light="0.5 0.85 0.3 -0.6">
        <Fragment slot="lead">Short, because this site collects very little. Last updated October 2026.</Fragment>
      </LPageHead>
    ) : (
      <PageHead kicker="Privacy">
        <Fragment slot="title">Privacy notice</Fragment>
        <Fragment slot="lead">Short, because this site collects very little. Last updated October 2026.</Fragment>
      </PageHead>
    )
  }

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose privacy">
      <p>
        This site is run by {site.name}. If you have a question about your information, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <p>
        Only what you choose to send: your name, email address and the answers you give in the enquiry form, including
        any link to your deck. If you email me directly, I receive whatever you include in that email.
      </p>

      <h2>Why, and on what basis</h2>
      <p>
        I use it to reply to your enquiry and, if we decide to work together, to scope and deliver the work. Under UK
        GDPR, the basis is taking steps at your request before entering into a contract, and my legitimate interest in
        responding to people who contact me.
      </p>

      <h2>Your deck</h2>
      <p>
        I ask for a view-only link rather than an attachment so that you stay in control of access. I read it myself,
        don’t share it, and use it only for your enquiry and any work we agree. You can revoke the link at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
      <p>
        The enquiry form is delivered to my inbox by a form service, which processes your answers only to pass them on.
        I don’t sell or share your information with anyone else, and I don’t use it for marketing lists.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site uses Plausible Analytics to count visits and see which pages are useful. Plausible doesn’t use cookies
        and doesn’t collect personal data; everything it reports is aggregated. This site sets no cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Only as long as I need it to respond and follow up, or for the length of any engagement and the records that
        go with it. I’ll delete it sooner if you ask.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see the information I hold about you, to correct it or to delete it, and you can object to how
        it’s used. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If you’re unhappy with how I’ve handled your
        information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>


  .privacy > p:first-child::first-letter {
    float: none;
    font: inherit;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .privacy {
      margin-left: calc(4 / 12 * 100% + 21px);
    }
  }
</style>
